# Each ignored finding needs a reason and a review date. Keep this list short.
#
# AVD-AWS-0107 / AVD-AWS-0104: security groups allow 0.0.0.0/0.
#   The ALB must accept public HTTP(S), and tasks need HTTPS egress to AWS APIs
#   because there is no NAT gateway or VPC endpoints (cost; ADR 0003). Review: 2026-12-01.
AVD-AWS-0107
AVD-AWS-0104
# AVD-AWS-0054: ALB listens on plain HTTP. Only when no certificate_arn is set (no domain yet);
#   with a certificate, HTTP redirects to HTTPS. Review: 2026-12-01.
AVD-AWS-0054
# AVD-AWS-0053: load balancer is internet-facing. That is its job: it's the public API.
AVD-AWS-0053
# AVD-AWS-0057: IAM wildcard resources. ecr:GetAuthorizationToken and
#   ecs:RegisterTaskDefinition/DescribeTaskDefinition don't support resource-level permissions;
#   the other ECS actions are narrowed with an ecs:cluster condition. Review: 2026-12-01.
AVD-AWS-0057
# AVD-AWS-0132: state bucket uses SSE-S3, not a customer-managed KMS key ($1/month per key).
#   Bucket is private, versioned, TLS-only. Review: 2026-12-01.
AVD-AWS-0132
